[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Module Requirements — config.py (Configuration Loading & Variables)
PREAMBLE: >>>
Design-level requirements for lib/config.py module.
Covers project configuration loading, role defaults, variable building,
substitution engine, and related operations.
Total: 15 requirements covering all functions in config.py.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONFIG-001
TITLE: load_project_config — Parse project.yaml
STATEMENT: >>>
Load project configuration from .meta-config/project.yaml:
  - name, version, tech-stack, providers (ai-providers)
  - custom_vars, role-overrides
  - lifecycle-triggers, provider-isolation setting
  - DoD preset, req-traceability flag
Return: Config dataclass with all fields validated.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Centralized config loading ensures consistent defaults and validation.
Single source of truth for project-wide settings.
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
- tests/test_config.py::test_load_project_config_valid
- tests/test_config.py::test_load_project_config_missing_required
- tests/test_config.py::test_load_project_config_invalid_yaml
<<<
TAGS: config, loading, validation, schema
STATUS: Active
PRIORITY: P1
OWNER: @daniel
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: implements
  VALUE: REQ-SYS-001
- TYPE: called-by
  VALUE: REQ-SYNC-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONFIG-002
TITLE: load_role_defaults — Parse role-defaults.yaml
STATEMENT: >>>
Load role configuration (model, memory, permissionMode, tier, temperature).
Format:
  roles:
    orchestrator:
      model: claude-opus-4-7
      memory: project
      permissionMode: allow
      tier: 0
      hint: Central coordination
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Centralized role configuration enables consistent role definitions across projects.
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
- tests/test_config.py::test_load_role_defaults_valid
- tests/test_config.py::test_load_role_defaults_missing_file
<<<
TAGS: config, roles, loading
STATUS: Active
PRIORITY: P1
OWNER: @daniel
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: called-by
  VALUE: REQ-SYNC-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONFIG-003
TITLE: build_variables — Assemble All Substitution Variables
STATEMENT: >>>
Merge variables from:
  1. project.yaml custom_vars
  2. role-defaults.yaml role names/descriptions
  3. DoD preset (DOD_*, if active)
  4. Computed (FRAMEWORK_VERSION, AGENT_HINTS, etc.)
  5. Environment (PROJECT_NAME, TECH_STACK, etc.)
Return: dict {VAR_NAME: value} for {{VAR}} substitution.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Unified variable assembly enables dynamic template rendering.
Variables come from multiple sources with clear precedence.
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
- tests/test_config.py::test_build_variables_all_sources
- tests/test_config.py::test_build_variables_precedence
<<<
TAGS: config, variables, building
STATUS: Active
PRIORITY: P1
OWNER: @daniel
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: calls
  VALUE: REQ-CONTEXT-001
- TYPE: called-by
  VALUE: REQ-SYNC-001, REQ-CONTEXT-005
- TYPE: refines
  VALUE: REQ-SYS-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONFIG-004
TITLE: substitute — Replace {{PLACEHOLDERS}} in Content
STATEMENT: >>>
Find all {{UPPERCASE_WITH_UNDERSCORE}} patterns and replace with variable values.
Pattern: [A-Z0-9_]+
Warn if unresolved placeholders remain in final output.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Regex-based substitution enables flexible templating without special syntax.
Warns on unresolved placeholders to catch config errors.
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
- tests/test_config.py::test_substitute_basic
- tests/test_config.py::test_substitute_unresolved_warning
- tests/test_config.py::test_substitute_escaped_braces
<<<
TAGS: config, substitution, variables
STATUS: Active
PRIORITY: P1
OWNER: @daniel
RELATIONS:
