  VALUE: REQ-SYS-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONFIG-005
TITLE: validate_project_config — Check Config Validity
STATEMENT: >>>
Validate project config against schema:
  - Required fields present (name, ai_providers)
  - Field values are correct types
  - Provider names are recognized
  - Custom variable names follow naming rules
Return: (valid: bool, errors: List[str]).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Schema validation catches configuration errors early.
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
- tests/test_config.py::test_validate_project_config_valid
- tests/test_config.py::test_validate_project_config_missing_required
- tests/test_config.py::test_validate_project_config_invalid_type
<<<
TAGS: config, validation, schema
STATUS: Active
PRIORITY: P1
OWNER: @daniel
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: called-by
  VALUE: REQ-CONSISTENCY-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONFIG-006
TITLE: resolve_model_for_role — Get LLM Model for Role
STATEMENT: >>>
Determine which LLM model to use for given role.
Priority: project.yaml override > role-defaults.yaml > global default.
Return: model string (e.g., "claude-opus-4-7").
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Model configuration enables per-role LLM selection.
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
- tests/test_config.py::test_resolve_model_for_role_override
