[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONFIG-009
TITLE: expand_variable_references — Resolve Nested Variables
STATEMENT: >>>
Resolve nested variable references: if {{VAR1}} = "hello {{VAR2}}",
expand to actual value of VAR2.
Single pass (no recursive resolution).
Return: variables dict with expanded values.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Nested variables enable composition of complex values.
Single-pass resolution prevents infinite loops.
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
- tests/test_config.py::test_expand_variable_references_nested
- tests/test_config.py::test_expand_variable_references_circular_detected
<<<
TAGS: config, variables, expansion
STATUS: Active
PRIORITY: P2
OWNER: @daniel
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: called-by
  VALUE: REQ-CONFIG-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONFIG-010
TITLE: validate_custom_variables — Check User-Defined Variables
STATEMENT: >>>
Validate custom_vars from project.yaml:
  - Names follow {{VAR_NAME}} pattern ([A-Z0-9_]+)
  - Values are strings or JSON-serializable
  - No reserved names (framework vars like FRAMEWORK_VERSION)
Return: (valid: bool, errors: List[str]).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Variable validation prevents naming conflicts and malformed references.
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
- tests/test_config.py::test_validate_custom_variables_valid
- tests/test_config.py::test_validate_custom_variables_invalid_name
- tests/test_config.py::test_validate_custom_variables_reserved_name
<<<
